# Themes, Volt UI & Routes

## View namespaces (not `resources/views`)

| Area | Path | Namespace | Helper |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Client | `resources/client_area/{theme}/` | `theme::` | `client_view()`, `client_view_path()` |
| Admin | `resources/admin_area/{admin_theme}/` | `admin::` | `admin_view()`, `admin_view_path()` |
| Email | `resources/email_templates/{email_theme}/` | `email::` | — |
| Invoices | `resources/invoices/` | `invoices::` | — |

Themes come from `config/app.php` (`theme`, `admin_theme`); default folder is `default`.

## Volt (preferred Livewire)

- Create **single-file** Volt components colocated in the theme, e.g. `resources/client_area/default/cart/livewire/view-cart.blade.php`.
- Pattern: `new class extends Component { ... }` then Blade markup in the same file.
- Mount with `@livewire(client_view_path('…'))` or `admin_view_path('…')` — not stock `resources/views/livewire`.
- Call `Model::actions()` from Volt methods; keep validation/errors user-facing.
- Activate `volt-development` + `livewire-development` skills when editing these files.
- Use Tailwind (not Bootstrap) unless the surrounding theme already uses something else.

## Routes

- Client: `routes/web.php` — names like `dashboard`, `cart`, `orders.view`, `payments.pay`.
- Admin: `routes/admin.php` — auto prefix `admin`, name `admin.*`, middleware `web,auth,admin,…`.
- Auth: `routes/auth.php` — prefix `auth`.
- Protect admin mutations with `middleware('permission:admin.…')` and Blade `@perm` / `@endperm`.

## Assets

- Client/admin static assets are published via `vendor:publish --tag=client` / `--tag=admin` (also on Composer dump). After theme CSS/JS changes, publish or ask the user to run build/`composer` scripts.
- Local URL via Herd: `http://wemx.test` (folder name).

## Layouts

- Extend `theme::layouts.wrapper` or `admin::layouts.wrapper`.
- Reuse Blade components under `resources/*/default/components/` as `<x-theme::…>` / admin equivalents before creating new ones.
